# Chapter 2, Step 3 — the application's OWN Kconfig options.
#
# A file named "Kconfig" in the application root is picked up by the
# build automatically. This is where the product defines the knobs
# that belong to IT (as opposed to CONFIG_* options that belong to
# Zephyr itself, which we only SET in prj.conf).
#
# The last line is mandatory in an application Kconfig file: it pulls
# in the rest of the Zephyr Kconfig tree.

menu "Room sensor demo"

config ROOM_BLINK_PERIOD_MS
	int "Sensor poll / heartbeat period (ms)"
	default 1000
	help
	  How often the main loop polls the simulated sensor. A product
	  tunes numbers like this without touching C code — prj.conf (or
	  a board-specific config fragment) just overrides the default.

config ROOM_FEATURE_HEARTBEAT_LOG
	bool "Print a heartbeat log line every period"
	default y
	help
	  A demo "feature switch": when this is off, the heartbeat code
	  is not merely skipped at runtime — it is compiled out of the
	  firmware entirely, because main.c tests it with IS_ENABLED().

endmenu

# Per-module log-level symbols for OUR OWN module do not appear by
# magic: they exist only where a Kconfig file instantiates Zephyr's
# log-config template for that module name. Zephyr's subsystems do
# this for their modules; this line does it for "sim", creating
# CONFIG_SIM_LOG_LEVEL_DBG and friends — which is what allows
# prj.conf to raise just this one module to DBG.
module = SIM
module-str = Simulated sensor (Chapter 2 demo)
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_config"

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
